<p>Port Arthur water damage claims often start small: a stain on the ceiling, a soft spot in the hallway floor, or a water heater that let go overnight. By the time the drywall is opened, the damage can reach several rooms. Insurers handle these claims carefully because the policy language around water is detailed. Whether the loss is covered usually comes down to three questions: where the water came from, how suddenly it happened, and how quickly it was stopped and dried. This page covers non-flood water losses. If rising water entered your home, see our <a href="/services/flood-damage-claims/">flood damage claims</a> page instead.</p>

