</tbody>
</table>
<p>Keep the failed part. A cracked fitting or split supply line is physical evidence of a sudden failure. Ask the plumber to write down what failed, where it was, and what they observed about how long it had been leaking. That short note is often more persuasive than anything else in the file.</p>

