<h2>Mitigation and Drying Come First</h2>
<p>Your policy almost certainly requires you to take reasonable steps to prevent further damage. In Port Arthur’s climate, that means moving fast. Wet drywall, insulation, and cabinets in a humid house can start growing mold within days, and insurers may limit payment for damage that spread because drying was delayed.</p>
<ol>
<li>Shut off the water at the fixture or main.</li>
<li>Photograph and video the source, standing water, and every affected room.</li>
<li>Call a water mitigation company to extract water and set drying equipment.</li>
<li>Ask for daily moisture readings and drying logs, and keep copies.</li>
<li>Report the claim promptly and keep a record of every conversation.</li>
</ol>
<p>Our <a href="/claim-documentation-checklist/">claim documentation checklist</a> includes a water-loss section.</p>

